The Doctor's Dream

In rural Bihar, Zara wanted to become a doctor. When child marriage pressure mounted, her mother sold her jewelry to fund Zara's education. "My daughter will heal others, not hide her potential," she said.

Despite financial struggles and social pressure, Zara studied medicine. Today, she runs a clinic in her village, providing affordable healthcare to girls and women who previously had no access to female doctors.

Her success inspired her community to educate their daughters.